# Core Table Reference

The installer creates the following core tables.

- `tblShops`: branch master.
- `tblUsers`: application users and role labels.
- `tblCategories`: product categories.
- `tblProducts`: product master, SKU/barcode, cost/selling prices, reorder level.
- `tblCustomers`: customer master and credit limit.
- `tblSuppliers`: supplier master.
- `tblStock`: quantity by shop and product.
- `tblPurchases`, `tblPurchaseDetails`: purchase headers and lines.
- `tblSales`, `tblSaleDetails`: sales headers and lines.
- `tblStockMovements`: auditable inventory movement log.
- `tblStockTransfers`, `tblStockTransferDetails`: inter-shop transfer.
- `tblIMEI`: unique mobile IMEI/serial register.
- `tblPayments`: receipts and payments.
- `tblExpenses`: shop expenses.
- `tblAuditLog`: application activity log.

All monetary values use Currency data type (PKR). Dates use Date/Time. Primary keys are AutoNumber. Foreign-key enforcement is intentionally limited in the initial installer so it can be extended without Access relationship conflicts; add and test relationships in Database Tools → Relationships before production.
